Third-party components
----------------------

libmpv
    Frame bundles and links against libmpv and uses the mpv render API
    (mpv_render_context / render_gl) to present video. libmpv is Copyright
    (C) the mpv project, licensed under the GNU General Public License
    version 2 or later (GPLv2+); the prebuilt binaries used here are built
    with GPL-enabled FFmpeg. FFmpeg terms depend on the components and build
    configuration. libmpv is linked dynamically and is bundled with Windows
    packages; Linux uses the distribution's libmpv package.

Qt 6.8
    Qt is Copyright (C) The Qt Company Ltd. and other contributors. Frame
    uses Qt 6.8 (Core, Gui, Qml, Quick, QuickControls2) under the GNU Lesser
    General Public License version 3 (LGPLv3). Qt is used exclusively as
    dynamically linked libraries; users may replace or relink against a
    modified Qt. Qt binaries were obtained via aqtinstall
    (win64_msvc2022_64, Qt 6.8.3).

Prebuilt binaries
-----------------
The binary was built against prebuilt libmpv development artifacts from the
zhongfly/mpv-winbuild project (mpv-dev-x86_64 builds) and Qt 6.8.3 binaries
installed with aqtinstall. Version details are recorded in
third_party/VERSIONS.txt.

Corresponding source
--------------------
The Frame application source is provided in this repository. Windows bundles
libmpv from the pinned upstream mpv-winbuild release listed in
third_party/VERSIONS.txt; it is dynamically linked. The upstream project and
its build records are at https://github.com/zhongfly/mpv-winbuild. Linux links
to the distribution's libmpv package. FFmpeg components and other libraries
are subject to their own licenses; see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and
docs/LICENSING.md for their upstream source and license information.

Qt's LGPL license text is included in licenses/LGPL-3.0-only.txt. Windows Qt
libraries are dynamically linked and remain replaceable. Qt source and
corresponding source terms are available at https://www.qt.io/licensing/
open-source-lgpl-obligations.
